# Scale & list UX defaults

When building or changing **any list/table/report** in LocalHyperMart portals (vendor, hub, admin, buyer history):

## Assume hundreds of rows

Do not ship a bare “map all rows” screen as the final UX. Default toolkit:

- **Pagination** (25/50 default; Prev/Next is enough)
- **Sort** on the columns people scan (date, amount, status, name)
- **Search / filter** for the primary identifier (order #, product name, phone, etc.)
- **Date or status scope** so the first load is not “all time, everything”
- **Collapse detail** (line items, nested rows) — summary first, expand on demand
- **Exports** may include the filtered set; say so if scoped

## Density

- Prefer one job per viewport (tabs over stacking two huge tables)
- Primary KPIs only up front; secondary metrics behind “more”
- Human labels (`New`, `Ready`) over raw enums in filters

## Backend

- Prefer server pagination/filter when payloads get large (items × orders).
- Until then, client page/sort/filter is required — never leave an unbounded scroll as the only control.

## Process

Apply this **without waiting for the user to ask again**. If a new list ships, it should already be searchable, sortable, and paginated unless there is a hard reason (e.g. fixed 5-item checklist).
